=== HINT 1: WSAStartup + resolve ===
WSADATA wsa;
WSAStartup(MAKEWORD(2,2), &wsa);

ADDRINFOA hints = {0}, *res = NULL;
hints.ai_family   = AF_INET;
hints.ai_socktype = SOCK_STREAM;
getaddrinfo("127.0.0.1", "4444", &hints, &res);

=== HINT 2: Create socket + connect ===
SOCKET s = socket(res->ai_family, res->ai_socktype, res->ai_protocol);
int conn = connect(s, res->ai_addr, (int)res->ai_addrlen);

=== HINT 3: Send beacon string ===
const char *msg = "BEACON\n";
int sent = send(s, msg, (int)strlen(msg), 0);

=== HINT 4: Cleanup ===
closesocket(s);
freeaddrinfo(res);
WSACleanup();

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
WSAECONNREFUSED (10061) is normal - no listener is running.
Beacon implants typically sleep between connections and use a loop:
  while (1) { connect(); send_check_in(); recv_task(); run_task(); sleep(interval); }
Real beacons randomize the sleep interval (jitter) to evade time-based detection.
WinINet / WinHTTP are higher-level alternatives that handle proxies and TLS automatically.
